# File: compiler/patches/agda-language-server-wasm-project.patch
#
# What: the server's wasm project file, cabal.project.wasm32, for the build
# of issue 58: the Hackage index at the Agda commit's time, the lsp and
# lsp-types of the server's own submodule (lsp 2.8.0.0, lsp-types 2.4.0.0)
# in place of the pinned lsp 2.7.0.1 and lsp-types 2.3.0.1, lsp's websocket
# flag off, and Agda's use-xdg-data-home flag stated off.
#
# Why: the reactor module (app/Reactor.hs) needs lsp 2.8's
# runServerWithConfig, and both variants are built from this one project
# file, so that they differ only in the reactor flag.  lsp 2.8's websocket
# support, on by default, brings websockets and through it entropy, whose
# custom Setup cannot configure for wasm32 ("unable to find library
# -lHSrts-1.0.2_thr"); the server does not use it.  The index state is
# the plain agda's, so the two plans differ only where the server's own
# dependencies require it (lsp caps aeson below 2.3, and Agda's project
# file, which the plain agda uses, takes splitmix from a fork).  Without
# use-xdg-data-home the server's data directory is $Agda_datadir itself,
# where the page puts lib/prim.
#
# Against: agda/agda-language-server 0f77a209243185cb8e36a11bfc7b6ab47f5125b4
# (tag v8).
#
diff --git a/cabal.project.wasm32 b/cabal.project.wasm32
index 4e37f38..41aba3c 100644
--- a/cabal.project.wasm32
+++ b/cabal.project.wasm32
@@ -1,13 +1,11 @@
-index-state: 2026-02-16T23:59:59Z
-
-constraints:
-  lsp == 2.7.0.1,
-  lsp-types == 2.3.0.1
+index-state: 2026-10-05T16:41:29Z
 
 packages:
   .
   wasm-submodules/agda
   wasm-submodules/network
+  wasm-submodules/lsp/lsp
+  wasm-submodules/lsp/lsp-types
 
 source-repository-package
   type: git  
@@ -21,4 +19,7 @@ source-repository-package
   tag: 2c3ab6e7aa2a86be692c55bf6081161d83d50c34
 
 package Agda
-  flags: +optimise-heavily
+  flags: +optimise-heavily -use-xdg-data-home
+
+package lsp
+  flags: -websocket
